      "function": "sc_pkcs15_decode_prkdf_entry",
      "line": 260,
      "code": "r = sc_asn1_decode_choice(ctx, asn1_prkey, *buf, *buflen, buf, buflen);",
      "note": "Attacker-controlled ASN.1 data from the fuzzer buffer is parsed. sc_asn1_decode_choice partially decodes the input and may internally allocate memory (via SC_ASN1_ALLOC) for info.subject.value before encountering an error and returning r < 0.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/libopensc/pkcs15-prkey.c",
      "function": "sc_pkcs15_decode_prkdf_entry",
      "line": null,
      "code": "sc_format_asn1_entry(asn1_com_prkey_attr + 0, &info.subject.value, &info.subject.len, 0);",
      "note": "sc_format_asn1_entry stores &info.subject.value (the address of the stack-local pointer field) into asn1_com_prkey_attr[0].parm. The error handler later uses parm as the argument to free, but parm is a pointer-to-pointer (stack address), not the heap pointer itself.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/libopensc/pkcs15-prkey.c",
      "function": "sc_pkcs15_decode_prkdf_entry",
      "line": 253,
      "code": "sc_format_asn1_entry(asn1_com_prkey_attr + 0, &info.subject.value, &info.subject.len, 0);",
      "note": "sc_format_asn1_entry stores &info.subject.value (the address of the stack-local pointer field) into asn1_com_prkey_attr[0].parm. The error handler later uses parm as the argument to free, but parm is a pointer-to-pointer (stack address), not the heap pointer itself.",
      "kind": "root_cause_line"
    },
    {
      "file": "src/libopensc/pkcs15-prkey.c",
      "function": "sc_pkcs15_decode_prkdf_entry",
      "line": null,
      "code": "free(asn1_com_prkey_attr[0].parm);",
      "note": "free() is called with asn1_com_prkey_attr[0].parm, which equals &info.subject.value — a stack address at offset 360 within the info local variable. ASAN detects this as a bad-free because the address was never malloc'd.",
      "kind": "sink_function"
    },
